(:taskCollection
  :id "Phase454EngineBindingGroundTruth"
  :createdAt 1789157400000
  :status "completed"
  :priorityOrder 2
  :summary "Engine Binding Ground Truth: module resolution driven by declared manifests instead of a path guess ladder, an unresolved import that is fatal and located, the 40 missing builtins including the control forms, and a re-measured corpus."
  :phase "Phase454EngineBindingGroundTruth"
  :baseline "Measured 2026-09-11 in D81StaticSweepAudit20260911: 136 of 313 suites exit non zero and every one of them is ERR_UNBOUND_SYMBOL, with zero assertion failures. 76 distinct symbols are missing: 40 bare builtins and 36 alias prefixes. resolveModulePath in the decoded evaluator is a hardcoded ladder of about 25 path guesses; the import branch has no else, so a module that does not resolve is skipped in silence and the error surfaces later at the call site."
  :tasks [
    (:task
      :id "Task45401"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-454"
      :title "Module resolution reads the declared module graph instead of guessing paths"
      :kind :engine
      :lane "binding"
      :state :done
      :priority :critical
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789157400000
      :updatedAt 1789250000000
      :motivation "The repository already declares 770 module names in (module NAME ...) headers, and the evaluator ignores every one of them. Resolution is a hardcoded ladder of about 25 candidate directories carrying package specific special cases, including a branch that rewrites the module name core to sql and a candidate under asl/web/src/data/blog. A module placed anywhere the ladder does not enumerate is unreachable no matter how correctly it is declared, and adding a package requires editing the evaluator."
      :purpose "Resolution is driven by an index built from the declared module headers: a module name resolves to the file whose header declares that name, and nothing else. The index is built once per run and is the same index the static tooling uses, so what the evaluator can bind and what the analyser reports can never diverge."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Module name to file index built from the declared headers" "The guess ladder and its package special cases removed" "Adding a package requires no evaluator edit" "Ambiguous duplicate module names are an error, not a first match"]
      :owns ["asl/tools/engine_js.h" "asl/tools/gen_engine_header.sh"]
      :targetSymbols ["resolveModulePath" "loadModuleImports" "moduleCache"]
      :relatedSymbols ["semantics" "foreign"]
      :invariants ["C3" "D34" "D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn []
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45401"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task45401.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A module in a directory absent from the old ladder resolves by its declared name." "Two files declaring the same module name is an error naming both paths, not a silent first match." "Resolution does not depend on the process working directory."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45401" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts []
      :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Build the module index from declared headers." "Replace resolveModulePath with an index lookup." "Make duplicate declarations an error." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 0
      :receipts [
        (:receipt :contract Task45401 :timestamp 1789250000000 :exitCode 0 :executedAsserts 4 :verdict :pass :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45401")
      ])
    (:task
      :id "Task45402"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-454"
      :title "An unresolved import is fatal and names the import, not a later call site"
      :kind :engine
      :lane "binding"
      :state :done
      :priority :critical
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789157400000
      :updatedAt 1789250100000
      :motivation "Measured: the import branch is guarded by a condition with no else, so a module that does not resolve is skipped without a word. The declaring module still evaluates, because a df body is not executed at definition time, and the failure appears much later as unknown builtin or function s/concat at whichever call site runs first. 52 of the 136 failing suites are mis-attributed this way: the message names a symbol the author never wrote as a builtin, in a file that is not the file with the defect. agent-bus/src/bus.asl imports core/strings, which exists nowhere outside a grammar fixture, and the reported failure is in agent-bus/tests/bus_test.asl."
      :purpose "An import that does not resolve fails at the import, with the importing file, the line, the module name as written and the candidate that was searched. No alias is ever bound to a module that was not loaded."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Unresolved import is fatal at the import site" "Diagnostic carries file, line, module name and search result" "The 52 mis-attributed failures re-attribute to their real cause" "No alias binds to an unloaded module"]
      :owns ["asl/tools/engine_js.h"]
      :targetSymbols ["loadModuleImports" "resolveModulePath"]
      :relatedSymbols ["semantics" "gates"]
      :invariants ["C3" "D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task45401"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45402"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task45402.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A module importing a name that resolves nowhere fails at that import, quoting the importing file and line." "The diagnostic never names a call site in a different file." "A suite whose only defect is an unresolvable import reports the module, not a symbol."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45402" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts []
      :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Add the else branch and the located diagnostic." "Re-run the corpus and record the re-attribution." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 0
      :receipts [
        (:receipt :contract Task45402 :timestamp 1789250100000 :exitCode 0 :executedAsserts 14 :verdict :pass :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45402")
      ])
    (:task
      :id "Task45403"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-454"
      :title "The 40 missing builtins, with case and match as real control forms"
      :kind :engine
      :lane "binding"
      :state :done
      :priority :critical
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789157400000
      :updatedAt 1789250200000
      :motivation "Measured: 40 distinct bare symbols that the corpus calls do not exist in the evaluator, and they are not exotic. They include fst, snd, second, reverse, append, join, fold-left, list-fold, list-filter, list-take, list-first, list-last, count, get, enumerate, nil?, map-merge, string-trim, string-trim-left, string-append, string-repeat, string-count-char, string-to-lowercase and the numeric conversions. Two of them, case and match, are control forms rather than functions, so the language the corpus is written in and the language the evaluator implements disagree about branching itself."
      :purpose "Every one of the 40 is implemented, with case and match as special forms evaluated before argument evaluation. The set is closed against the corpus: after this task no suite fails on a bare symbol, and any remaining bare failure is a genuine authoring error."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["40 builtins implemented" "case and match are special forms" "Zero bare-symbol failures remain across the corpus" "Each builtin carries a behavioural test, not a presence test"]
      :owns ["asl/tools/engine_js.h" "asl/grammar/language-semantics.asn"]
      :targetSymbols ["evalNode" "invokeClosure"]
      :relatedSymbols ["semantics" "names"]
      :invariants ["C3" "D51" "D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task45401" "Task45402"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45403"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task45403.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["case does not evaluate the branches it does not take." "fold-left folds left and is distinguishable from a right fold on a non commutative operator." "list-take past the end returns the whole list rather than failing." "A builtin present but wrong fails the case; presence alone does not pass it."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45403" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts []
      :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Enumerate the 40 against the grammar." "Implement, control forms first." "Behavioural case per builtin." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 0
      :receipts [
        (:receipt :contract Task45403 :timestamp 1789250200000 :exitCode 0 :executedAsserts 34 :verdict :pass :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45403")
      ])
    (:task
      :id "Task45404"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-454"
      :title "refute as a first class falsification primitive"
      :kind :engine
      :lane "binding"
      :state :done
      :priority :high
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789157400000
      :updatedAt 1789250300000
      :motivation "refute appears in the corpus as a called symbol and does not exist in the evaluator. The whole protocol rests on a gate that must fail before it passes, and the primitive that expresses must fail is missing, so every falsification is currently written as an inverted assert by hand or is not written at all."
      :purpose "refute takes an expression and passes only when that expression fails or returns non true, and it is counted separately from assert so a suite reports assertions and refutations distinctly. A refute over an expression that raises is a pass; a refute over an expression that returns true is a failure naming the expression."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["refute implemented and counted separately" "Suite output distinguishes assertions from refutations" "The twelve case kinds in docs/TEST_CASE_CATALOG.md can be expressed without hand inversion"]
      :owns ["asl/tools/engine_js.h" "docs/TEST_CASE_CATALOG.md"]
      :targetSymbols ["assertionCount" "evalNode"]
      :relatedSymbols ["gates" "hiddenTests"]
      :invariants ["D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task45403"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45404"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task45404.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A refute over a true expression fails the suite." "A refute over a raising expression passes and is counted as a refutation." "A suite of refutations only still reports a non zero executed count."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45404" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts []
      :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Implement refute and its counter." "Extend the catalogue." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 0
      :receipts [
        (:receipt :contract Task45404 :timestamp 1789250300000 :exitCode 0 :executedAsserts 14 :verdict :pass :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45404")
      ])
    (:task
      :id "Task45405"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-454"
      :title "The 22 files that use an alias they never declare"
      :kind :remediation
      :lane "binding"
      :state :done
      :priority :high
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789157400000
      :updatedAt 1789250400000
      :motivation "Measured: 22 failing suites call a module qualified symbol while declaring no import at all, and a further 30 declare imports that do not include the alias they then use. These are genuine authoring defects that the silent resolver has been hiding, and they cannot be separated from resolver defects until Task45402 makes unresolved imports fatal."
      :purpose "Every qualified symbol in the corpus is backed by a declared import whose module resolves. Where the intended module cannot be determined from the code, the call is recorded as an open question rather than guessed at."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Every qualified symbol has a declared, resolving import" "Undeterminable intents recorded rather than guessed" "agent-bus/src/bus.asl no longer imports a module that exists only as a grammar fixture"]
      :owns ["agent-bus/src" "agent/src" "agent-core/src" "asl/packages/asl-codec/tests" "intel/src" "harness/src"]
      :targetSymbols ["bus" "csv-transpile" "sh-transpile"]
      :relatedSymbols ["foreign" "semantics"]
      :invariants ["C3" "D34" "D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task45402"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45405"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task45405.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A qualified symbol with no matching declared alias fails a repository wide check." "An import naming a module that exists only under asl/grammar/corpus fails." "The check runs over the whole corpus, not over a sample."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45405" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts []
      :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Enumerate qualified symbols against declared aliases." "Repair where intent is determinable." "Record the rest." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 0
